From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Vishnefske <jvishnefske@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:27:26 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] std: run std's unit tests on linux-none

Make the in-crate unit tests (library/std/src/**/tests.rs) build and
link without libc on linux-none, and run the ones that were left out:

- process/unix/common/tests.rs calls kill, getpgid, pthread_sigmask,
  sigemptyset and sigaddset from libc: give it a small libc module of
  its own on rt's syscalls, with libc's conventions.
- net/tests.rs (ZeroedMmap) and os/unix/net/tests.rs (close, getpid,
  getuid, getgid) call rt directly on linux-none.
- The pidfd tests run against linux-none's PidFd (which also uses its
  current_process and pid, otherwise dead in a test build).
- test_named_thread_truncation reads the thread's name back with
  prctl(PR_GET_NAME), there being no pthread_getname_np.
